  "claim": "A South American company produced its first film in 2006. The star of the film won Best Young Actor/Actress at the 2004 Broadcast Film Critics Association Awards. The company also produced Alien Invasion Arizona.",
  "evidencia": "Page: The Nativity Story. Sentence: The Nativity Story is a 2006 biblical drama film based on the nativity of Jesus, directed by Catherine Hardwicke and starring Keisha Castle-Hughes and Oscar Isaac.\nPage: Keisha Castle-Hughes. Sentence: The film was nominated for many awards, including an Academy Award for Best Actress (at the time the youngest person nominated in the Best Actress category) and an award at the Broadcast Film Critics Association Awards for Best Young Actor/Actress, which she won in 2004.\nPage: Temple Hill Entertainment. Sentence: The first film company produced was \"The Nativity Story\" in 2006 by director Catherine Hardwicke.\nPage: Alien Invasion Arizona. Sentence: It is also entitled \"The Salena Incident\" and was a straight to DVD release produced by Temple Hill Entertainment and distributed by Lionsgate.",
